753__x8ce315__Grit-Bros/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-221150__xaf71fe__Boiler-Buddies/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-221209__x8e2f53__Pitfall-ish-The-Understory-Pitfall-II-Lost-Caverns/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-221213__x33c9c4__Pit-and-Away-Lost-Caverns-Pitfall-II-Lost-Caverns/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-221223__xc30db2__Pitfallin-Pitfall/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-221447__x70cd8b__Pit-Perfect-Pitfall/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-221659__x2d1181__Short-Order-Fever-Pressure-Cooker/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-222023__xc8da9d__Pressure-Buns-Pressure-Cooker/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-222101__xa8fd04__Raiders-of-the-Lost-Fortune-Raiders-of-the-Lost-Ark/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-222300__x1d6bdf__Raiders-of-the-Lost-Hieroglyph-Raiders-of-the-Lost-Ark/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-222441__xde02fc__River-Razzle-River-Raid/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-222451__x63fa06__Solar-Flair-Solaris/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-222851__xf51be0__Solaris-Detour/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-223041__x8fa92a__Stellar-Raiders-Star-Raiders/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261105-224539__xc2682b__Star-Riders-Star-Raiders/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011135__x71288e__Upstream-Uproar/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011141__xdc36f6__The-Empire-Strikes-a-Detour/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011147__xe109ac__The-Empire-Bites-Frost/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011153__x1d9df2__Super-Bounceout-Super-Breakout/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011159__x8f4f7d__Super-Breakbeat-Super-Breakout/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011205__x28a79e__Son-of-a-Sun/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011211__x32f31f__Super-Delivery/\n?? ../../gpt-6.1-sol-ultra__20261106-011217__x3c28c7__Paddle-Royale-Video-Olympics/\n\n/home/micha/AGENTS.md\n# AGENTS.md — Workstation environment for AI coding agents\n\n> Home-level instructions for any coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, opencode, grok, agy, aider)\n> on this box. Linked as every agent's *global* rules file, so it applies inside any repo; repo-level\n> `AGENTS.md` files override it. Only things you **cannot infer**. Keep < 10 000 chars (grok truncates).\n> Last optimized: 2026-09-23. Full history/rationale: `~/AI-DEV-SETUP.md`.\n\n## Environment (the non-obvious bits)\n\n- **Ubuntu 26.04 on WSL2**, 20 cores, **16 GB RAM cap** (`.wslconfig`). **`/tmp` is a 7.9 GB RAM tmpfs** —\n  put big builds/caches under the project or `~/.cache`, never `/tmp`.\n- **No Linux GUI** (WSLg disabled on purpose). GUI checks: `xvfb-run -a`; Android: headless emulator +\n  screenshots. **Don't launch GUI `.exe`s** via interop — they pop up on the user's desktop.\n- **sudo requires a password** (ask Michael — never guess/hardcode). Default to userspace installs:\n  `mise use -g <tool>@latest` · `uv tool install <pkg>` · `npm i -g <pkg>` · `cargo binstall <crate>`.\n\n## PATH — one file, every shell\n\n- **`~/.config/ai-dev/env.sh`** is the single source of PATH/toolchain env, sourced last by `~/.profile`\n  (so `bash -lc` agents get it) and `~/.bashrc`. Add PATH entries **there**, not in rc files.\n- Precedence: `~/.local/bin` > mise shims > JDK 21 > nvm node > cargo/bun/dotnet/flutter/android/go\n  > system > **Homebrew last** (brew duplicates ~200 system bins — python3, git, glib tools — and once\n  hijacked `node`; never `brew install node`, never prepend brew).\n- **Windows PATH is filtered to an allowlist** (system32, PowerShell, WindowsApps, `code`, `cursor`,\n  `gsudo`); Windows dev-tool shims otherwise shadow missing Linux tools. Windows toolchains:\n  `cmd.exe /c \"<cmd>\"` or `powershell.exe -NoProfile -Command \"<cmd>\"`. Full PATH: `AI_DEV_KEEP_WINPATH=1`.\n- Pagers are neutralized for agents (`PAGER=cat` etc.). `rg` is pre-configured (`~/.ripgreprc`).\n\n## Installed toolchain — do NOT reinstall (check `command -v` first)\n\n- **Runtimes:** node **24 LTS** (nvm default; 22 kept), bun, deno, python 3.14, go 1.27, rust 1.98,\n  **JDK 21** (`JAVA_HOME`=brew `openjdk@21`; brew's `java` 27 is shadowed on purpose), kotlin, gradle,\n  maven, **.NET 10** (`~/.dotnet`), **Flutter 3.47/Dart 3.13** (`~/.local/opt/flutter`), zig, gcc 15,\n  clang 21 (system; brew LLVM 23 only for `clangd`/`clang-tidy`), cmake, ninja, meson.\n- **Mobile/desktop:** Android SDK `~/Android/Sdk` (API 36+37, build-tools 37, NDK 30, emulator, AVD\n  `pixel8_api37`, **`android` CLI**), Chrome, `eas`, `tauri`, `maestro`, `cargo-xwin`, mingw-w64, nsis,\n  GTK/WebKitGTK dev libs, rust targets (android, windows-gnu/msvc, wasm32).\n  → **Read `~/.claude/skills/app-platforms/SKILL.md` before any mobile or desktop app work.**\n- **Pkg/env mgrs:** `uv` (prefer over pip), `pipx`, pnpm/yarn (corepack), `mise`, `cargo binstall`.\n- **Search/nav:** `rg`, `fd`, `ast-grep` (alias **`sg` shadows the system `sg`** — use `/usr/bin/sg`),\n  `fzf`, `zoxide`, `ctags`.\n- **Data/HTTP:** `jq`, `gron`, `xh`, `curl`, `7zz`, `parallel`. ⚠ **two `yq`s:** `yq` = python/kislyuk\n  4.x (jq syntax, `-y` for YAML out); the Go/mikefarah one is **`yq-go`** (`yq-go -o=json '.a'`).\n- **QA:** `ruff`, `ty`, `biome`, `eslint`, `oxlint`, `prettier`, `shellcheck`, `shfmt`, `pre-commit`,\n  `semgrep`, `tokei`, `hyperfine`, `knip`, `cspell`.\n- **Browser tests:** Playwright for **Python** (1.63) is a pipx venv: run scripts that `import playwright`\n  with `~/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python` (system `python3` can't import it). Browsers are\n  in `~/.cache/ms-playwright`; if WebKit reports missing host libraries: `sudo ~/.local/bin/playwright install-deps webkit`.\n- **Other:** `repomix`, `files-to-prompt`, `llm`, `just`, `watchexec`, `sqlite3`, `psql`, `redis-cli`,\n  `pandoc`, `dot`, `direnv`, `git` 2.53 + `git-lfs`, `gh` (authenticated), `docker` (native engine,\n  user in group), `kubectl`, `helm`, `terraform`, `vercel`, `ollama` (GPU, qwen2.5-coder).\n- **Agents on PATH:** `claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `opencode`, `grok`, `agy`, `aider`, `jules`.\n\n## Node / npm gotchas\n\n- **npm 12 blocks two things by default** (the install still \"succeeds\"):\n  (a) dependency **install scripts** — native/binary-downloading deps end up broken. Fix per project:\n  `npm approve-scripts <pkg>` (writes `allowScripts` in package.json) then `npm rebuild <pkg>`;\n  globals: `--allow-scripts=<pkg>` (allow-listed ones: `npm config get allow-scripts`).\n  (b) **git-URL dependencies** (`EALLOWGIT`) — e.g. Electron Forge. Fix: `allow-git=all` in the\n  project `.npmrc`; scaffolders: `npm_config_allow_git=all npx create-electron-app …`.\n- Keep `nvm alias default` an **exact** version (env.sh reads it without loading nvm). New node via\n  nvm starts with no globals: `nvm reinstall-packages <old>`. Don't `npm config set prefix`.\n- Global `tsc` is pinned to **5.9.3** (TS 7 ships no `tsserver`; `typescript-language-server` needs it).\n  The native 7.x compiler is `tsgo`. Repos pinning their own `typescript` are unaffected.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- **Search:** lexical `rg` → structural `ast-grep --lang <l> -p '<pattern>'` → language LSP.\n- **GitHub/git: use `gh`/`git` CLIs, not MCP** (far fewer tokens, already authenticated).\n- **Python:** `uv run`, `uv add`, `ruff check --fix && ruff format`, `ty check`. No bare `pip`.\n- **JS/TS:** `biome check --write` when the repo has no formatter configured.\n- **Shell scripts you write:** `shellcheck` + `shfmt -w`. Never `pkill -f <pat>` when `<pat>` is in your\n  own command line — it kills your own shell.\n- **Verify before claiming done:** run the repo's own test/build commands (`justfile`, `package.json`\n  scripts, `Makefile`, `pyproject.toml`).\n- **Parallel work:** git worktrees (`gwt <branch>` in interactive shells, or `git worktree add`).\n\n## Language servers (all verified with a real LSP `initialize`, 2026-09-23)\n\n| Language | Server | Typecheck / compile |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| TS/JS | `typescript-language-server` | `tsc` 5.9.3, `tsgo`, `eslint`, `oxlint`, `biome` |\n| Python | `pyright-langserver` | `ty`, `mypy`, `pyright`; `ruff` lint/format |\n| Go · Rust · C/C++ | `gopls` · `rust-analyzer` · `clangd` | `go vet` · `cargo check` · gcc/clang, cmake |\n| Java · Kotlin | `jdtls` · `kotlin-lsp` | `javac`/gradle · `kotlinc`/gradle |\n| C# · Dart/Flutter | `csharp-ls` · `dart language-server` | `dotnet build` · `dart analyze`/`flutter analyze` |\n| Bash · YAML · Lua · Markdown | `bash-language-server` · `yaml-language-server` · `lua-language-server` · `marksman` | `shellcheck` · — · — · `markdownlint` |\n| JSON/CSS/HTML | `vscode-{json,css,html}-language-server` | `biome`, `stylelint` |\n\nIf `rust-analyzer` says *\"Unknown binary … in official toolchain\"*: `rustup component add rust-analyzer`.\n\n## Skills (shared across agents)\n\n- `~/.claude/skills/` is the source of truth (grok reads it directly); each skill is also linked into\n  `~/.codex/skills`, `~/.config/opencode/skills`, `~/.gemini/skills`, `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills`.\n- **app-platforms** (mobile + desktop), **game-toolchain** (Blender/Godot/texture/audio — read before any\n  3D/2D/sprite/audio/Godot work), **android-cli** (official; refresh with `android init`).\n  Imagine art (sprites, animation, tiles, UI, GLB) is the bundled skill **game-assets**. Do not merge it with **game-toolchain**.\n\n## MCP servers — keep it lean\n\n- >10 MCP servers measurably degrades agents. Connected for Claude: **Context7** (live library docs —\n  use it instead of guessing current APIs) plus productivity integrations.\n- Add a coding MCP **only when a CLI can't do the job**, per project (e.g. browser automation:\n  `claude mcp add chrome-devtools -- npx -y chrome-devtools-mcp@latest`). Android UI inspection\n  needs no MCP: `android layout` / `android screen`.\n- MCP servers run as this user: pin versions, prefer vetted servers, keep a human in the loop for\n  writes/sends/deletes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
