{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '150,380p' vendor/engine/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n- Background: `r.sky(['#top', '#mid', '#bottom'])`, `r.starfield({ count, speed, dir: 'down' | 'left' })`.\n- Depth sorted: `r.actor(x, y, z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view), { flash: '#ffffff', flashMix: .75, alpha, xray, outline, ghost, emissive, every, key })` (the flash tints over the sprite so shading shows: `flashMix` .5 by default, 1 solid; `every: 2, key: npc` redraws a background character every other frame; actors up to about 250 px tall), `r.sprite(x, y, z, sprite, { flip, anchor: 'bottom' | 'center', glow, flash })`, `r.queue(x, y, z, g => {...}, { bias })` (sorted by that one point: a long wall by `r.queueSpan(a, b, z, h, fn)`), `r.actorNow(...)` (as `r.actor`, drawn at once over what is drawn so far), `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)` (inside a queue function). `{ pick: unit }` on any of them (and `r.shape`), then `r.pick(sx, sy)` → what the last frame drew under a screen point, front to back.\n- Floor marks: `r.shadow(x, y, radius, alpha, color, surfaceZ)`, `r.decal(g => r.groundArc(...))`, `r.groundDisc`, `r.groundRing`, `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n, z)`.\n- On top, unlit, screen pixels: `r.text(str, x, y, color, { align, scale, outline })`, `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color)`, `r.overlay(g => {...})`.\n- `r.w(x, y, z)` = buffer pixel of a world point. `r.W`, `r.H`, `r.ix`, `r.iy` (pass to dither functions), `r.view`, `r.visible(x, y, z)`.\n- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high (22; `hides: true | false` says otherwise) or anything queued with `{ hides: true }` is drawn in front of it; not by one rising less than 8 above its feet (the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall). `xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors: true }`: with `actors` other bodies in front hide it too (a hero stays findable in a crowd). Afterimages: `ghost: { color, life, alpha, owner }`; `owner` (the actor's `{x, y, z}`) keeps a trail left nearer the camera sorted behind the live body.\n- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\n\n## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\n- Sprites from strings (for coins, bullets, ships, icons, NES-style enemies): `const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }, scale)`. `.` and space are transparent. Frames: `const walk = E.anim([f1, f2, f3], 8, { pingpong })` (or one sheet: `E.anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 })`), drawn with `r.sprite(x, y, z, walk, { t })`. `r.sprite(..., { rot: angle, scale })` turns and scales in whole pixels (cached in 16 steps a turn; `steps: 32`); `E.recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a' })` swaps a palette.\n- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case: ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, the accented Latin letters; any other is `?`; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n- UI (inside `r.overlay(g => ...)`): `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, gradient, alpha })` (a gradient window like Final Fantasy; `bg` can be `[top, bottom]`, `gradient: false` for flat, `alpha: .6` for a see-through HUD panel), `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, color)`, `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max)` (half hearts allowed), `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg, frame, cape: false, weapon: false, tint: '#808080' })` (character close-up; it stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down; `tint` greys out a KO'd hero).\n- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while a modal box is open: play waits); in draw `talk.draw(r)`. `portrait` takes a Humanoid (live close-up; `portraitSize: 40`, `portraitOpts: { zoom, turn }`) or a function `(g, x, y, size) => {...}`. Radio chatter during play: `talk.say('Enemy fighters ahead!', { name, portrait, auto: 2.5, modal: false })` turns its pages and closes by itself while the game keeps running. Per line: `place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom'`, `y` (pixels) and `alpha` (see-through box). `new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars })` (`voice`: a sound, or `(ch, i, talk) => {}` per letter); `talk.close()`, `talk.open`. Markup in the text: `{c=#ffd36a}gold{/c}` a color, `{w=.5}` a pause, `{s=12}slowly{/s}` letters a second, `{shake}..{/shake}`, `{wave}..{/wave}`, `{$name}` a value from `say(text, { vars })` or `talk.vars`.\n- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel, scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (rows: it scrolls); `menu.update(dt)`; `menu.draw(r)`. Keys, d-pad and sticks move it; a click or tap on an entry picks it (so a phone can leave a title), and the mouse over one moves the cursor. A tap on a dialog box turns its page as confirm does.\n- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { scale: 2 } (a TV; or `tv: true`), settings, screens: { pause, help, dev: { rows: ['glyphs'] } } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'map' | ..., spec)`; each step `ui.hud({ objective, status, bars, prompt, minimap })` (`minimap: { map, fog, camera: true, markers, onClick(x, y) }`); `ui.toast(title, text)`.\n\n## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n- `sfx(name, { vol, pitch, pan, loop })` → `{ stop(), set({ pan, vol }) }` (a loop sounds on: an engine, rain). Presets: `jump jump2 land step coin pickup key powerup oneup heal hit hurt stomp bump swing whoosh punch kick shoot laser charge explode boom door secret warp die select confirm cancel pause text blip`.\n- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`; `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` is a `wave` too.\n- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen). Your own Web Audio connects to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, under the volume and mute.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time, headless too, and the sound follows it. `music(song, { sync: true })` pauses with the game (else it plays on); `audio.pos` → `{ t, step, beat, bar, at, loop, bpm, layers, playing }`; `at(step, fn)`, `onBeat(fn)` (on the update step); `tempo(bpm)`; `layer(name or index, vol, fade)` (a track's `name`, `on: false` starts it silent: the chase's drums in by layers); `music(song, { fade: 1 })` crossfades; `sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` over the music; `sfx(voice, { step })` on a step of the music. `settings.audioOffset` (ms, Settings, Sound: Calibrate) sets `audio.offset`; `audio.calibrate()` → `{ tap(), result, done, stop() }`.\n\n## Levels\n**TileMap** (top-down, isometric, brawler): walls stand on the ground plane.\n- `new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorTex, block: ['water', 'lava'], ao: 5, outside })` (`ao` = width of the contact shadow along wall bases, 0 = none; `outside`: the ground past the map, a color, or `false` for none). `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut: true, cutH, face, roof, beam }` (`cut` lowers walls that block the camera, those `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)` says; a map may replace it; `face`: `'brick'` (default) `'stone' 'rock' 'plank' 'timber' 'plaster' 'hedge' 'none'`; `roof`: `'speckle'` (default) `'plain' 'tiles' 'slab' 'leaves' 'grass'`; `beam` = timber color). `floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view)` returns `[r, g, b]` (or `[r, g, b, glow]`); ready-made: `E.tex.flagstone`, `grass`, `dirt`, `water`, `planks`, `checker`, `plain`. A map of more than 128 x 128 cells bakes its floor in squares as the camera comes to them and lets the far ones go (`chunks: true | false` to choose; `map.floorBytes()` what it holds), so a 256 x 256 world map costs what the screen shows.\n- Legend values: a number = wall type, a string = spawn tag, `{ tile, floor, spawn, block }` for both. `block: true` (or the map's `block` list of floor tags) makes deep water, lava or pits stop walkers (jumping bodies pass over); `walkable(cx, cy)`, `block(cx, cy, on)` (a bridge appears). FlowField paths go around blocked cells and follow `block` and `set` at their next `update`.\n- `find(tag)` / `findAll(tag)` give `{ x, y, z, cx, cy }`. Also `cell(cx, cy)`, `set(cx, cy, id)` (open doors), `toCell(x, y)`, `center(cx, cy)`, `heightAt(x, y)`, `floorAt(x, y)`, `groundAt(x, y, r, z)`, `collide(body)`, `los(x0, y0, x1, y1)` (ground only), `bounds(view)` (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, buffer pixels), `drawFloor(r)`, `queueWalls(r)`.\n\n**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `eye` / `chest` override them (crouching). Same level: `|dz| <= 8`. On a TileMap (`dir` = an angle or `[dx, dy]`): `ray(a, b, { eye, target })` → `{ clear, t, x, y, z }`, `sight(a, b)`, `standable(x, y, z, r)`, `ledge(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, rise, facing, edge }` (climb), `landing(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, d }` (a jump across a gap), `drop(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, fall }`, `arcClear(a, b, apex, r)`, `pick(sx, sy)` → `{ cx, cy, z, face }` (the cell under a screen point: `input.clicked()`, any view and turn). Helpers: `E.sameLevel(a, b)`, `E.targets(from, list, { range, arc, dz, sight: map })` → `[{ target, d, dz, angle }]` nearest first, `E.inArc(..., dz)`. `new E.FlowField(map, { climb, drop, jump })` paths over roofs, between levels and across gaps.\n\n**PlatformMap** (side-scrollers; 2.5D in tilted views): tiles on the x/z plane, top row first.\n- `new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types })`. `types[id] = { kind, style, side, top, line, mat }` (`mat`: any material for a solid tile's face). Example: `rows: ['      ?    ', '   ===     ', '@  g   ^^  ', '###########']`, `legend: { '#': 1, '=': 2, '?': 3, '^': 4, '@': 'hero', 'g': 'walker' }`, `types: { 1: { style: 'ground', side: '#8a5a32' }, 2: { kind: 'oneway' }, 3: { style: 'bonus', side: '#e8a830' }, 4: { kind: 'hazard' } }`. Kinds: `'solid'` (default), `'oneway'` (jump up through), `'ladder'`, `'slope'` (`dir: 1` rises to the right, `-1` to the left; `from` / `to` heights 0..1 for gentle slopes), `'hazard'` (spikes, lava), `'deco'`, `'back'` (background wall). Styles: `'stone'` (`moss`) `'brick' 'wood' 'metal' 'ground'` (`flower`) `'block' 'pipe' 'bonus' 'plank' 'spikes' 'ladder' 'liquid' 'plain'`.\n- Spawns: `find(tag)` gives `{ x, z }` with z = the bottom of that cell (feet). Standing on the ground means z = the top of the floor tiles (`level.groundBelow(x, z)`, which returns `null` over a pit), not z = 0. `cell(cx, cz)` / `set(cx, cz, id)` count cz from the bottom row. `slopeZ(cx, cz, x)`, `touching(body, 'hazard')`, `cellsTouching(body, kind)`, `groundBelow(x, z)`, `solidAt(x, z)`, `move(body, dt, solids)`, `bounds(view)`, `draw(r)` (call first, after `r.sky`), `width`, `height`.\n\n## Movement and physics\n**Platformer** (side-scroller character): `const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22, run: 95, jump: 285, gravity: 800, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, dash: 0 })`.\n- Each update: `hero.update(dt, level, game.input, movingPlatforms)`. For enemies pass `{ x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }` instead of the input.\n- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\n- Built in: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height (let go early for a short hop), slopes and small steps (sticks to the ground going down), ladders (up / down), drop through one-way tiles (down + jump), optional double jump, wall jump and dash.\n- Further moves, each on request: `crouch` (down: half as tall, it crawls), `ledge` (catches a ledge falling past it; up climbs), `wallCling`, `momentum` (slopes, a roll, a charged dash); tile kinds `'water'` (it swims), `'rope'` (up grabs it), `'bars'` (it hangs and travels), grip `friction` (ice .15), `carry` (a conveyor), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` and `respawn` (`level.update(dt)` each step); `hero.swingFrom(x, z)` (a grapple: a pendulum, jump lets go); draw `level.drawWater(r)` after the actors. State: `crouching`, `hanging`, `clinging`, `swimming`, `onRope`, `onBars`, `swinging`, `rolling`; `rigState()` poses them.\n- Moving platforms: `{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }` boxes you move yourself and pass as `solids`; riders are carried.\n\n**Body** (top-down / isometric / brawler): `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 5, friction: 0, bounce: 0, gravity: 700 })`. Set `vx`, `vy`, then `body.update(dt, map)`. Also `push(ix, iy, iz)` (knockback), `jump(v)`, and `onGround`, `z`, `groundZ`, `hitWall`, `landed`, `bounced` (hit the ground and bounced: dust, a thud). Walls lower than your feet are walkable, so bodies can jump onto blocks.\n\n**Mover** (third person): `const mover = new E.Mover({ x, y })`; `mover.update(dt, map, game.input)` (input `'THIRDPERSON'`) or an AI's `{ move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }`: it sprints, sneaks, climbs, vaults, leaps gaps, hops down and rolls; `climbAny: true` climbs any wall (jump at it; up the screen is up the wall; jump leaps up, crouch lets go; `mover.wall`, `map.wall(from, dir)`), `glide: true` glides (jump again in the air; `lift`: an updraft), `staminaMax: 100` (climbing, gliding and sprinting spend `mover.stamina`); `rig.update(dt, mover.rigState())`; `mover.play('takedown', { other })`, your own `E.ACTIONS`. Stealth: `E.sees(guard, hero, { map })` → `{ seen, exposure }`, `E.hears`, `new E.Suspicion()` (`update(dt, seen, hero)` → `'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'`), `r.sightCone(guard, { map })`, `r.marker(x, y, z, { label })`.\n\n**Attack** (melee timing for swords, punches, kicks): `const slash = new E.Attack('slash')` (a move from `E.MOVES`, optionally with overrides: `new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 })`) or a spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, wind, active, recover }`. `if (input.buffered('attack') && slash.start()) input.consume('attack')`; `slash.update(dt)` (returns the phase that just began); `slash.hits(enemies, e => E.inArc(hero, facing, e, 22, 1.4), e => {...})` hits each target once per swing during `'active'` (moves wait until `hitAt: .35` of the swing, so hit-stop freezes the strike, not the wind-up); `rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: slash.state })`. Also `busy`, `active`, `cancel()`. **Combo**: `const combo = new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut'], { window: .3 })` (names, specs or Attacks); `combo.press()` starts or chains the next hit; `update`, `hits`, `state`, `step` work the same. **Knockback**: `E.knockback(attacker, target, 160, up)` pushes a Body (or anything with vx / vy) away.\n\n**Bullets**: `const shots = new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side' })`; `shots.fire({ x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r: 2, team: 'player', color, life, dmg, pierce, sprite })`; `shots.burst(base, E.pattern.spread(angle, n, arc, speed))`; `shots.update(dt, map)`; `shots.hit(targets, (b, t) => {...}, 'player')`; `shots.draw(r)`; `shots.clear(team)`. Patterns: `E.pattern.dir(angle, speed)`, `aim(a, b, speed)`, `aimSide(a, b, speed)`, `spread(angle, n, arc, speed)`, `ring(n, speed, offset)`. In side view the second number of a pattern velocity is vz.\n\n**Helpers**: `E.dist(a, b)`, `E.angleTo(a, b)`, `E.arc(a, b, gravity, { apex | time | speed })` → `{ vx, vy, vz, t }` (a throw that lands at b: a lob, a grenade), `E.overlap(a, b)` (circles x, y, r), `E.overlapBox(a, b)` (side boxes x center, z feet, w, h), `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)` (melee cone; `dz` limits the height difference), `E.rand(a, b)`, `E.randInt(a, b)`, `E.pick(list)`, `E.chance(p)`, `E.prune(list, fn)`, `E.store.get(key, fallback)` / `set(key, value)` (save data; slots: `game.saves`), `new E.SpatialHash(32)` (`build(list)`, `near(x, y, r, fn)`), `new E.FlowField(map)` (`update(tx, ty)` or `update([[x, y], ...])`: the nearest; `dir(x, y, tx, ty)` walks around walls and `map.solid` shapes), math `clamp lerp approach ease.* angDiff approachAng smoothDamp rng(seed) noise2 hex shade mix`; `E.version` (the release) and `E.versionLabel()` ('v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': show it on a title or a debug screen).\n\n## Characters\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists) | a game's own (`E.Humanoid.weapon(id, { length, rest, draw(w) })`; `.hat(id, draw)`, `.pose(id, (J, w) => ...)`; `draw: { under, over }`; state `tilt`, `roll`), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat. `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above the feet), `flip: 0..1` (a roll), `land: k` (a heavy landing); `mover.rigState()` sets them. Every wind-up starts from the rig's current pose, so chained hits and hand changes never snap. Idle rigs breathe and shift their weight by themselves.\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\n| Real-time strategy (Warcraft II, StarCraft, Dune II) | `iso` | `E.Strategy` (the strategy module): kinds as data, selection by click, box and group, orders, gold, building, training, fog, an AI's build order and waves; `cam.free`, `{ pick: unit }` and `r.pick`, buildings as `E.SHAPES`, E.Shell's minimap; bodies drawn `every: 3` | RTS |\n| Theme park or city sim (Theme Park, RollerCoaster Tycoon, SimCity) | `iso` | paths as floor tags walked on an `E.Grid`, agents with `E.needs` picking by `E.choose`, `E.Clock` days and light, `game.timeScale` 0 to 4, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`; rides as shapes stepped through angles (`params`, `facing`) | SIM |\n| 3D platformer or adventure remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash) | `iso` / `threequarter` / `brawler` | TileMap blocks of different heights + Body `jump()` (z is real height); in real 3D: `E.World3D` (the 3D engine's manual), `camera.lock` | ADVENTURE; 3D ACTION, 3D PLATFORMER |\n| Survival horror (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark) | the 3D engine's `'zones'` camera | `camera.zones` (fixed cameras by room), `camera.steer` (tank controls), `camera.lock` to aim, `world.through` doors, `world.flashlight`, fog; `E.RPG` inventory, `game.saves` | 3D HORROR |\n| First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) | the 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes | cells of 2 x 2 tiles stepped and turned a quarter at a time (tweened), `E.Grid` paths for the monsters, `E.Turns` `'atb'` (real time) or `'speed'` (turns), `E.Fog` for the automap, `world.thing('door')` gates and `world.unlock`, `rig.drawPortrait` for the party | 3D CRAWLER |\n| Rhythm (Dance Dance Revolution, PaRappa, Beatmania, Space Channel 5) | any (a highway on the overlay) | `E.Rhythm` (the rhythm module): a chart of lane strings in parts on a song's steps, judged in ms of the music clock, combo, life, grade, holds, calls a teacher plays and you answer, `rh.draw` (`arrows: true`); the songbook's songs (`E.Songbook`); lanes as `input.zones` on a phone; `audio.onBeat` moves the dancer | RHYTHM |\n| Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam) | `threequarter` / `topdown` | the ball an `E.Body` (`bounce`; curl: turn its velocity across its path), passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` for a lob, a shot's meter, formations by where the ball is, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` | SPORTS |\n| Third-person stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu) | `iso` / `threequarter` | TileMap roofs, Mover, `E.sees`, `E.Suspicion`, FlowField `jump` | STEALTH |\n| Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero) | Mode 7 (the mode7 module, over any view) | `E.Mode7` over a TileMap track (floor tags: grass, sand, boost), `E.Car` karts (`kart: true`: hop, drift, boost) in an `E.Race` round an `E.Path` (laps, checkpoints, drivers, items), rigs in karts as billboards, `game.splitScreen(2)` for two | KART |\n| 3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.track` (banked, walls, pads, `gaps` for a shortcut), `world.vehicle` karts raced by `E.Race`, split screen through `world.cameras` | 3D RACING |\n| Rail shooters (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.flyer` on rails or free in bounds, rolls (`f.rolling`) turn shots aside, `f.seek` for a charged lock, `Dialog`'s radio | 3D FLIGHT |\n| Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Road Rash) | the pseudo-3D road (the road module) | `E.Road` segments (curves, hills, tunnels), scenery and traffic placed on it, `curveAt` throwing the car outward, a clock and checkpoints | ROAD |\n| Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA) | `topdown` / `iso` | `E.Car` on a TileMap (its floor tags slow it, its walls bounce it), `E.Race` for laps and drivers, cars drawn with `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points | KART |\n| First-person shooter (Doom, GoldenEye 007, Apex Legends) | the 3D engine's first person (or third) | a level of text rows or a terrain, `world.ray` hitscan, recoil and reloads, doors (`world.thing('door')`), raiders on `world.flow()` | 3D SHOOTER |\n| Bomberman, Frogger, Sokoban, Gauntlet, Robotron; Sonic, Prince of Persia; light guns | as the recipe says | `AI_GUIDE.md`'s Genre recipes: each on the kit closest to it | (a recipe) |\n\n**Sizes:** heroes 40-60 px tall at 320x240 (`size: 1.2-1.4`), bosses 1.8-2.4. Small things (coins, bullets, ships, pickups) are string sprites designed at 8-16 px, drawn at scale 2 if they are the player's ship. Keep hitboxes smaller than the art.\n\n**Feel numbers** (world units per second, tile = 16): walk 70-90, run 95-140, jump 250-320 with gravity 800, fall cap 330, dash 200-260, bullets 250-320 (player) and 70-120 (enemy), enemy walk 25-45. Hit feedback: `game.hitFx` (Effects).\n\n## More: animation and examples outside this card\nThe repo (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge; any file at `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`) holds more to take from. Its files are large: search them and take only what the game needs. Real 3D (`E.World3D`: first person, racing, flight) is there: `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`.\n- **Motion clips**: 325 curated and 2,548 motion-capture takes that play on any Humanoid: find one in `src/mocap/catalogs/`, cut a small set with `tools/anim-set.mjs`, then `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Where to find more; `docs/MOCAP.md`).\n- **Objects and materials** (full engine): `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws a still object from any view and facing, `map.solid(...)` makes it solid; `E.MATERIALS` dresses floors (`floorMat`), walls (`face`, `roof`) and platform tiles (`mat`). `docs/ASSETS.md` is the card: the format, the library, writing one and checking it with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`.\n- **Worked examples**: Emberdeep (`src/emberdeep/`), a whole game on this engine: 29 monster, boss and dummy bodies, 3 heroes and 30 skills, registered with `def(kind, id, spec)` (one search lists them); adapt them, they lean on the game's own helpers. `docs/CHARACTERS.md` is the recipe for a new body.\n- **Modules** (`engine/modules/<name>.js`; `modules/` in the handoff package): general systems in files of their own, each a `<script>` after the engine, its header its manual (read it there, or its section of the index). A kit carries the modules its slice names (`@modules` in its header); the full engine (`dist/my-3d2dge.js`; `my-3d2dge.js` in the handoff package) carries them all.\n  - `grid`: square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges over heights and past allies, fields of view, `E.Fog`, groups, shapes of effect, threat maps, `E.GridMover`, `E.Turns` (speed, charge time, phases, ATB). ROGUELIKE, PUZZLE, TACTICS, ARCADE, ARTILLERY, RTS, SIM, 3D CRAWLER.\n  - `gen`: generated maps from a seed: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes, Poisson scatter, as ASCII rows a TileMap reads. ROGUELIKE, ARCADE.\n  - `fight` (the full engine only): one-on-one fighting: `E.Fighter` (frame data, hurt boxes from the rig's joints, guards, throws, cancels, juggles, specials by motion or charge, a meter, projectiles), `E.Match` (rounds, KO, the HUD, training), `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`. FIGHTING.\n  - `rooms`: a world of rooms on a grid of screens (`E.World`): walking between them at open edges, the explored map (`drawMap`, or `shellMap()` for `E.Shell`), gates that abilities or keys open, saves in `E.store`. METROIDVANIA.\n  - `mode7`: the SNES's Mode 7 (`E.Mode7`): a camera over a flat floor (a TileMap's, a function's or a canvas), a turning sky, billboards far to near (rigs, sprites, shapes, your drawing), fog, `project` and `toFloor`, split screens. KART.\n  - `road`: the pseudo-3D road (`E.Road`): segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, tunnels, scenery and cars scaled by distance and hidden past a crest, the sky's parallax on curves. ROAD.\n  - `drive`: cars on the ground plane (`E.Car`: grip and slide, a kart's hop and drift boost, floor tags, walls and cars it bounces off) and races (`E.Race`: checkpoints along an `E.Path`, laps, places, drivers that pass and rubber-band, items, the HUD; the 3D engine's `world.vehicle` too). KART.\n  - `story`: dialogue as data (`E.Story`): lines with speakers and portraits, choices with conditions, flags and values, gotos, the game's events, a quest log, balloons over heads, a backlog, auto and skip; its state for a save. RPG, POINT-AND-CLICK, TACTICS.\n  - `rpg`: a role-playing game's rules (`E.RPG`): items, bags (slots or a grid of sizes), members with stats, levels and gear, status effects, a party (items used, rewards shared), shops, damage, random encounters by zone, list and card windows. RPG, 3D HORROR.\n  - `strategy` (the full engine only; needs `grid`): `E.Strategy` for real-time strategy (selection by click, box and group; queued orders; formations; production, resources, placement; fog, the minimap; an AI's build order and waves) and for sims `E.Clock` (days, the light), `E.needs` and `E.choose`, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`. RTS, SIM.\n  - `click` (the full engine only): point-and-click adventures (`E.Click`): painted rooms, walk areas with holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots with verbs, SCUMM's nine verbs, Sierra's icons, a verb coin or two buttons, an inventory, rules as data, exits, `story`'s talk; taps on a phone. POINT-AND-CLICK.\n  - `physics`: 2D rigid bodies (`E.Physics`): circles, boxes, polygons, segments, chains and arcs; bounce, friction, sensors, layers, sleep; fast balls swept, never passing through; the same world at any refresh rate; flippers, bumpers, slingshots, kickers. PINBALL, ARTILLERY.\n  - `terrain`: destructible ground in the side plane (`E.Terrain`): carved and added by circles and polygons, the ground below a point and its normal, rays for shots, walkers on slopes, a collider for `physics`. ARTILLERY.\n  - `songs`: the songbook (`E.Songbook`): songs by mood (field, town, battle, race, horror, chase, dance ...) and jingles (stage clear, game over, level up); `get(id)`, `find(mood)`. RHYTHM.\n  - `rhythm` (the full engine only): `E.Rhythm`: charts on a song's steps, judgments in ms of the music clock, combo, score, a life gauge, grades, holds, call and response, a note highway in any direction. RHYTHM.\n  - `arcade`: the coin-op's frame: scores that float up, extra lives, two players taking turns, credits and a continue, high-score tables with initials on a letter wheel, stage cards, the attract mode (a demo, the table, the title). ARCADE, SHOOTER, PINBALL.\n- **Everything running**: https://my-3d2dge.vercel.app/labs\n\n## Before you hand the game back\n- One IIFE starting with `const E = My3D2dge` (between the markers in a single file; `game/game.js` in the handoff package). Only your game: no leftover starter menu or unused slices. No network, no libraries.\n- Title screen and game-over screen as scenes; `pausable: true` on gameplay scenes. No pause, settings, rebinding or full-screen code of your own (they're standard); prompts from `game.input.label(action)`.\n- The camera follows the player (`game.focus` every update) and shows the level; the HUD uses screen pixels, or `E.Shell`'s HTML for a modern game (the STEALTH kit; the handoff package's template).\n- Sound effects on jump, hit, pickup and death; music per scene.\n- The look target list above: backdrop, textured tiles, props, sized and dressed HD characters, effects, title font, lights. Compare your screenshots with Symphony of the Night or Metal Slug, not with NES games.\n- If you can run commands: `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html` (your page; add `#scene` to jump to a scene). It presses start, plays, cycles the views, prints how much of the screen is filled and how many colors it uses, adds look notes (flat areas, checkerboard dithering, low contrast, a thin palette), and fails on any error. Act on every look note. `node tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html#scene --steps \"wait:1500 press:Enter wait:800 rec:16:2 press:KeyJ\" --crop x,y,w,h` records an animation frame by frame into one contact sheet: check every attack with it (a swing must wind up, strike, and settle back without jerks or backward sweeps).\n- Animation variety: every character has its own moves from `E.MOVES` (not one shared swing), enemies telegraph with a visible wind-up, and reactions play out (hurt, knockback, `down`, victory `cheer`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '116,151p' vendor/engine/API.md && sed -n '365,510p' vendor/engine/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '116,151p' vendor/engine/API.md && sed -n '365,510p' vendor/engine/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"\n## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n- Tweens (Phaser's): `game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat, yoyo, onDone, keep })` eases numbers on game time: paused with the game, slowed by `timeScale`, ended by a scene change unless `keep`. Returns `{ done, cancel() }`. `E.ease` has Penner's set: `linear`, `inSine` `outSine` `inOutSine`, `inQuad` `outQuad` `inOutQuad`, the same for `Cubic`, `Back`, `Elastic`, `Bounce`.\n- Scripts (Unity's coroutines) for cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials:\n```js full-script\ngame.script(function* () {\n  yield 1;                                   // seconds of game time\n  yield E.until(() => door.open);            // a condition\n  yield game.tween(boss, { y: 80 }, 1.5);    // a tween (or another script, or a generator) finishing\n  for (let w = 0; w < 3; w++) { spawnWave(w); yield E.any([8, () => enemies.length === 0]); }\n});\n```\n  `E.all([...])` waits for all; a bare `yield` waits one step. It runs at once to its first `yield`, the same at any refresh rate; `{ keep: true }` outlives the scene; `.cancel()`, `.done`, `.value`.\n- Paths: `const p = new E.Path([[x, y, z], ...], { closed, smooth: 'catmull' })`: `p.length`, `p.at(d)` (`{ x, y, z, angle }` by distance along: moving platforms, dives, rails), `p.nearest(x, y)` (a racer's progress), `p.draw(r)` to see it.\n- Weather: `game.weather = { kind: 'rain' | 'snow' | 'ash' | 'leaves' | 'sand', amount: .8, wind: .3, lightning: .2 }` (null: clear) falls through the world in every view, settles or splashes, flashes and thunders; cosmetic only (its own random stream), and it ends with the scene: set it in `enter`.\n- Wrap-around (Asteroids): `x = E.wrap(x, 0, W)`, `E.wrapDiff(a, b, W)` (the short way across the seam), and `wrap: [W, H]` on `r.sprite` or `r.actor` draws a copy across each edge.\n\n## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\nWith no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, a screen filter, the frame rate and its readout), **controls** the player rebinds (conflicts said first; dead zone, invert aim and move, button symbols, vibration; touch button side, size, opacity), **full screen** (a phone's first tap, a top-right button, the menu; turning it off is remembered), a **menu button** at the top right (on a touch screen it stays in play: it is the touch START), a **way out** of every menu screen, the **back gesture** stepping back in the game (`game.back()`) before it leaves the page, **pausing** when the page is hidden or the controller unplugs, and a page set up for phones (safe areas, no scrolling, zooming or pull to refresh on the canvas).\n- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`, `touch: 'never'` (a phone is told a controller or keyboard is needed). `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the screen (or null): keep a HUD clear of it.\n- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | 'load')` opens the screen from your own menu. Blocked storage keeps them for the visit.\n- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation' }]` (a standard key without a label sets its default). A canvas title's OPTIONS: `game.menu('settings')`. From code: `game.settings.set(key, v)`, `game.fullscreen.toggle()` (from a key, click or tap), `game.pause(reason)`, `game.resume()`. `live: true` (or `game.menu(name, { pause: false })`): menus over a world that keeps stepping (online play).\n- **Boot**: heavy setup in steps behind a boot screen, and a report for any error before play: `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title, steps: [['Building the city', () => { map = build(); }]] } })` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Boot).\n\n## Input: `game.input`\n- Actions in every preset: `up down left right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad), `start` (Enter, Start), `pause` (Escape, P, Start), `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z, pad A), `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B).\n- DEFAULT adds `attack` (J, X, click), `dash` (Space, Shift, K), `skill` (L, E, right click), `jump` (Z). PLATFORMER: `jump` (Space, Z, K, pad A), `attack` (X, J, click), `dash` (Shift, C, L), `skill`. SHMUP: `fire` (Space, Z, J, click), `bomb` (X, K). THIRDPERSON: `sprint` (Shift), `jump` (Space), `crouch` (C, Ctrl), `interact` (E, F), `attack` (J), `block` (K), `dodge` (L), `use` (Q), `map` (M, Tab).\n- `down(a)`, `pressed(a)`, `released(a)`, `repeat(a, delay, rate)` (menus), `buffered(a, win)` + `consume(a)`, `consumeAll()`, `anyPressed()`, `move()` (screen direction `[x, y]`, length up to 1), `use(preset)`, `touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'])`, `touchSet('confirm', 'TALK', near)` (a context button: relabel it, or hide it while it has nothing to do).\n- Moves: `input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing })` is true on the step a quarter circle forward and punch ends (numpad notation, mirrored when `facing` is -1: `'623'`, `'41236'`); `input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down+right', 'attack'], { window: .5 })` any run of inputs (a cheat code); `input.history` the last second of them (`{ t, dir, pressed }`, for an input display).\n- Players (two to four on one machine): `game.players` is `[game.input, ...]`, each an input with this API, its `player` number, `name` (`'P2'`), `color` (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and device. `game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin: (input, n) => {} })` lets them in: Start on a free gamepad, or 2 on the keyboard (player 2 takes its right half: arrows, `.` `/` `,` and the numpad; player 1 keeps WASD with F G H; a preset's `halves: { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: {...} }` its own); `game.addPlayer({ pad: 0 })` or `({ keys: 'right' })`, `game.removePlayer(p)`. Prompts, the pause (P2 PAUSED), a lost controller and the Controls screen are per player. One screen: `cam.frame(heroes)`. Split: `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [h1, h2], layout: 'auto' })` (`'columns'`, `'rows'`, `'grid'`; up to 4) draws the scene once per viewport (`r.viewport` is `{ i, x, y, w, h }`), then `scene.hud(r)` once over the whole screen; `game.viewports[i].follow(t)` or `.focus(x, y)`.\n- `clear()` releases held inputs, pending presses, virtual sticks and touch buttons; focus loss does this automatically. `suppress(a)` blocks an action for the current tick; `suppressCode('Mouse0')` lets a HUD widget consume that mouse button while other devices bound to the action still work.\n- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same; the right stick is `PadRAxisUp/Down/Left/Right`, the wheel `WheelUp`/`WheelDown`; `value(a)`: 0 to 1 (a trigger's travel, a stick's push). Options while Create is held is no press (the AI Hub's chord).\n- Touch settings: `touchEnabled`, `stickSide` (`'left'` or `'right'`), `stickRadius` (CSS pixels), `touchFilter(event)` (return false to reserve a canvas tap for UI). `touchArea()`: where the touch buttons cover the screen (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, or null): keep a prompt clear of it. `clicked()`: where a click or tap on the canvas landed (`[x, y]` in screen pixels) the step after it, else null; `pointer()`: the mouse in screen pixels; `drag()`: how far the stick's finger moved this step (`[dx, dy]`, or null), to steer one to one; `steer = 'drag'`: a finger anywhere steers, no stick drawn (`stickOn`: a finger is on it). `zones = [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }]` (fractions of the canvas): a finger in one holds its act until it lifts (a pinball's halves). Gestures (a mouse or one finger, screen pixels): `box()` → `{ x0, y0, x1, y1, done }` (a left drag; on touch a long press, then a drag), `longPress()`, `doubleTap()`, `pan()` → `[dx, dy]` (a finger's drag on open ground, a middle or right drag), `zoomPoint()`; `feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch, button, id })` plays a pointer in a test. `bindButtons(root)` wires `[data-act]` elements.\n\n## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n- Background: `r.sky(['#top', '#mid', '#bottom'])`, `r.starfield({ count, speed, dir: 'down' | 'left' })`.\n        const wall = (x, y) => !!cells[y] && cells[y][x] === '#';\n        for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n          const c = cells[y][x], X = bx + x * C8, Y = by + y * C8;\n          if (c === '#') {\n            if (cl) { px.col(g, '#2121de'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + 2, C8, 1); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) g.fillRect(X, Y + C8 - 3, C8, 1); if (!wall(x - 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + 2, Y, 1, C8); if (!wall(x + 1, y)) g.fillRect(X + C8 - 3, Y, 1, C8); }\n            else { px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, '#1c4a22'); if (!wall(x, y - 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, 2, '#5aa84a'); if (!wall(x, y + 1)) px.rect(g, X, Y + C8 - 2, C8, 2, '#0c2410'); if (E.hash2(x, y) < .3) px.dot(g, X + 2 + (x * 3) % 4, Y + 3 + (y * 5) % 3, '#7ac860'); }\n          } else if (c === '-') px.rect(g, X, Y + 3, C8, 2, cl ? '#ffb8ff' : '#e0a0ff');\n          else if (!cl) px.rect(g, X, Y, C8, C8, (x + y) % 2 ? '#141026' : '#171230');\n        }\n      });\n      // the seeds, lanterns and the berry: glowing (they stay bright under the light)\n      r.queue(0, -1e4, 0, g => {\n        for (const k of seeds) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 3, Y = by + y * C8 + 3; px.rect(g, X, Y, 2, 2, cl ? '#ffb897' : '#ffe9a0'); if (!cl) px.dot(g, X, Y, '#ffffff'); }\n        if (Math.floor(t * 4) % 2 || readyT > 0) for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k), X = bx + x * C8 + 4, Y = by + y * C8 + 4; if (cl) px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#ffb897'); else { px.blend(g, .45, 'add', () => px.disc(g, X, Y, 6, '#ffb030')); px.disc(g, X, Y, 3, '#fff4c0'); } }\n        if (berry) { const X = bx + 14 * C8 + 4, Y = by + TUN * C8 + 4; px.disc(g, X - 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.disc(g, X + 2, Y + 1, 2, '#e02a3a'); px.dot(g, X - 2, Y, '#ffb0b0'); px.rect(g, X - 1, Y - 3, 3, 1, '#4ad84a'); }\n      }, { emissive: true, bias: -1e6 });\n      if (!cl) { L.add(pos(hero.m).x, pos(hero.m).y, 8, 60, 1.2, { color: '#ffe890' }); for (const k of power) { const [x, y] = cellOf(k); L.add(X0 + x * C8 + 4, Y0 + y * C8 + 4, 6, 26, .7, { color: '#ffb040' }); } }\n      if (inter) { drawInter(r); return; }\n      // you: a lit sphere with a chomping mouth (classic: the flat yellow disc); dying, the mouth opens until you are gone\n      const hp = pos(hero.m), ang = Math.atan2(hero.dir[1], hero.dir[0]), open = hero.dying > 0 ? Math.PI * (1 - hero.dying / 1.5) : (hero.m.moving || hero.chomp > 0 ? Math.abs(Math.sin(t * 16)) : .3) * .9;\n      if (hero.dying <= 0 || open < Math.PI * .98) r.actor(hp.x, hp.y, 0, (g, x, y) => {\n        y -= 0; const R = 4;\n        if (cl) px.disc(g, x, y, R, '#ffe000'); else { px.disc(g, x, y, R, '#d8a010'); px.disc(g, x - .5, y - .5, R - 1, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x - 1.5, y - 1.5, 1.5, '#fff8c0'); }\n        if (open > .05) px.poly(g, [[x, y], [x + Math.cos(ang - open) * 7, y + Math.sin(ang - open) * 7], [x + Math.cos(ang) * 8, y + Math.sin(ang) * 8], [x + Math.cos(ang + open) * 7, y + Math.sin(ang + open) * 7]], cl ? '#000000' : '#141026');\n      }, { outline: !cl, rim: false, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n      if (deathT > 0) return;\n      for (const w of wisps) {\n        const p = pos(w.m), blink = w.blue && fright < 2 && Math.floor(t * 6) % 2, body = w.blue ? (blink ? '#f0f0ff' : '#2a3aff') : w.c;\n        if (w.eyes || cl) r.actor(p.x, p.y, 0, (g, x, y) => {\n          if (!w.eyes) { px.disc(g, x, y - 1, 4, body); px.rect(g, x - 4, y - 1, 9, 4, body); for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) px.dot(g, x - 3 + i * 3 + (Math.floor(t * 8) % 2), y + 3, '#000000'); }\n          if (w.blue && !w.eyes) { px.rect(g, x - 2, y - 2, 1, 2, '#ffd0c0'); px.rect(g, x + 2, y - 2, 1, 2, '#ffd0c0'); return; }\n          const [dx, dy] = w.m.dir; px.rect(g, x - 3, y - 3, 3, 3, '#ffffff'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y - 3, 3, 3, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, x - 2 + dx, y - 2 + dy, '#2a2aff'); px.dot(g, x + 2 + dx, y - 2 + dy, '#2a2aff');\n        }, { outline: false, rim: false, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n        else {   // a Blob rig, its colour its own (blue while you can eat it), its eyes on the way it goes\n          const rig = w.rig; rig.C.base = body; rig.C.dk = E.shade(body, -.35); rig.C.lt = E.shade(body, .35);\n          rig.update(1 / 60, { look: w.m.dir, walk: 1, squash: Math.sin(t * 10 + w.i) * .08 });\n          r.actor(p.x, p.y + 3, 0, (g, x, y) => rig.draw(g, x, y, E.VIEWS.threequarter), { outline: true, rim: true, wrap: [MW * C8, 0] });\n          if (w.blue) L.add(p.x, p.y, 6, 22, .5, { color: '#6a7aff' });\n        }\n      }\n      if (readyT > 0) r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, 'READY!', X0 + MW * C8 / 2, Y0 + (HY + 6) * C8 + 1, '#ffe040', { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#000' }));\n    }\n    function drawInter(r) {\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        const a = inter, y = Y0 + TUN * C8 + 4, x = X0 + a.x;\n        E.font.text(g, 'INTERMISSION', X0 + MW * C8 / 2, Y0 + 8 * C8, '#ffe070', { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#000' });\n        if (!a.big) { px.disc(g, x, y, 4, '#ffe040'); px.disc(g, x - 20, y - 1, 4, '#ff4a4a'); px.rect(g, x - 24, y - 1, 9, 4, '#ff4a4a'); }\n        else { px.disc(g, x + 30, y - 1, 4, '#2a3aff'); px.rect(g, x + 26, y - 1, 9, 4, '#2a3aff'); px.disc(g, x, y, 11, '#ffe040'); px.poly(g, [[x, y], [x - 12, y - 6], [x - 12, y + 6]], '#000000'); }\n      });\n    }\n    return {\n      id: 'maze', label: 'MAZE', res: [232, 270], about: 'EAT EVERY SEED, DODGE FOUR WISPS', hue: ['#ffe040', '#4ae8ff', '#ff4a8a'], touch: [], extra: [10000], light: .5,\n      begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; over = false; level = 1; inter = null; wisps = wisps || null; build(); reset(); },\n      revive() { over = false; reset(); },   // after a continue: the same maze, everyone back in place\n      force() { over = true; },\n      step, draw, box: () => [X0, Y0 - 12, MW * C8, MH * C8 + 22], edges: () => [X0 - 4, X0 + MW * C8 + 4],\n      get over() { return over; }, get level() { return level; },\n      state: () => ({ hero: [hero.m.cx, hero.m.cy], wisps: wisps.map(w => [w.m.cx, w.m.cy, w.eyes, w.blue]), seeds: seeds.size + power.size, level, fright: +fright.toFixed(3) })\n    };\n  })();\n\n  /* =================================== 2. FORMATION =================================== */\n  const FORM = (() => {\n    const FW = 224, FLY = 130;   // the field's width (its height is the screen's: FH), a moth's speed along its path (px/s)\n    let FH = 270;\n    const MOTH = {\n      a: E.sprite(['..y..y..', '.yYyyYy.', 'ybbBBbby', 'bbBwwBbb', '.bBBBBb.', '..b..b..'], { y: '#ffe040', Y: '#fff8a0', b: '#4a8aff', B: '#8ab8ff', w: '#ffffff' }),\n      b: E.sprite(['r......r', '.rRRRRr.', 'rRwRRwRr', '.rRRRRr.', 'r.r..r.r'], { r: '#e03a4a', R: '#ff8a8a', w: '#ffffff' }),\n      boss: E.sprite(['..gGGg..', '.gGwwGg.', 'gGGGGGGg', 'gpGppGpg', '.p.pp.p.', 'p......p'], { g: '#3ad860', G: '#9af0a0', w: '#ffffff', p: '#c050f0' }),\n      hurt: E.sprite(['..pPPp..', '.pPwwPp.', 'pPPPPPPp', 'pgPggPgp', '.g.gg.g.', 'g......g'], { p: '#a050e0', P: '#d8a0ff', w: '#ffffff', g: '#3ad860' })\n    };\n    const SHIP = E.sprite(['...w...', '...w...', '..wrw..', '.wwrww.', 'wwbwbww', 'w.bbb.w', 'r..r..r'], { w: '#f0f0f8', r: '#ff4a4a', b: '#4a8aff' });\n    const ROWS = [['boss', 4], ['b', 8], ['b', 8], ['a', 10], ['a', 10]];\n    const SLOTS = ROWS.flatMap(([kind, n], row) => Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => ({ kind, x: FW / 2 + (i - (n - 1) / 2) * 18, y: 36 + row * 16 })));\n    let cab, demo, foes, shots, bombs, ship, wave, sway, dead, over, readyT, stars = [], X0 = 0, Y0 = 0;\n    // a wave: five groups of eight fly in from alternate sides, a loop on the way, each to its own place (Catmull paths)\n    function newWave() {\n      foes = []; wave++; cab.card('STAGE ' + wave, 1.8); readyT = Math.max(readyT, .6);\n      SLOTS.forEach((s, i) => {\n        const group = Math.floor(i / 8), side = group % 2 ? 1 : -1, k = i % 8;\n        const path = new E.Path([[FW / 2 + side * 150, -20], [FW / 2 + side * 70, 80], [FW / 2 - side * 20, 170], [FW / 2 - side * 70, 120], [FW / 2 - side * 30, 70], [s.x, s.y]], { smooth: 'catmull' });\n        foes.push({ kind: s.kind, hp: s.kind === 'boss' ? 2 : 1, slot: s, path, d: -(group * 1.6 + k * .14) * FLY, state: 'in', x: path.at(0).x, y: -20, a: Math.PI / 2 });\n      });\n    }\n    function begin(c, isDemo) { cab = c; demo = !!isDemo; wave = 0; over = false; shots = []; bombs = []; sway = 0; dead = 0; readyT = 1.4; ship = { x: FW / 2, y: FH - 28, cool: 0 }; stars = Array.from({ length: 90 }, (_, i) => ({ x: (i * 97) % FW, y: (i * 53) % 600, s: 20 + (i % 3) * 25 })); layout(); newWave(); }\n    // a dive: from its place a swoop out, at the ship (where it is now) and off the bottom; it comes back from the top\n    function dive(f) {\n      const sx = ship.x, out = f.x < FW / 2 ? -1 : 1;\n      f.path = new E.Path([[f.x, f.y], [f.x + out * 30, f.y - 16], [f.x + out * 46, f.y + 20], [sx + (Math.random() - .5) * 50, FH * .62], [sx + out * 40, FH + 24]], { smooth: 'catmull' }); f.d = 0; f.state = 'dive';\n    }\n    const kill = f => { f.hp = 0; cab.add(f.kind === 'boss' ? (f.state === 'dive' ? 400 : 150) : f.kind === 'b' ? (f.state === 'dive' ? 160 : 80) : (f.state === 'dive' ? 100 : 50), { x: X0 + f.x, y: Y0 + f.y }); P.sparks(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 10); P.bits(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 6, ['#ffe040', '#4a8aff', '#ff4a4a']); A.sfx('explode', { vol: .45 }); };\n    function step(dt, I) {\n      layout(); sway += dt; ship.y = FH - 28;\n      for (const s of stars) s.y = (s.y + s.s * dt) % 600;\n      if (readyT > 0) readyT -= dt;\n      if (dead > 0 && (dead -= dt) <= 0) { const was = cab.p, r = cab.die(); if (r === 'over') { over = true; return; } if (r === 'next') { was.save = { wave, foes }; const s = cab.p.save; if (s) { wave = s.wave; foes = s.foes; for (const f of foes) if (f.state !== 'form') { f.state = 'back'; f.y = -20; } } else { wave = 0; newWave(); } } ship.x = FW / 2; bombs.length = 0; readyT = 1.4; }\n      const live = dead <= 0 && readyT <= 0;\n      if (live) {   // the ship: left and right; two shots on screen at most\n        const mv = demo ? botMove() : I.move()[0]; ship.x = clamp(ship.x + mv * 115 * dt, 10, FW - 10); ship.cool -= dt;\n        if ((demo ? botFire() : I.down('fire')) && ship.cool <= 0 && shots.length < 2) { shots.push({ x: ship.x, y: ship.y - 8 }); ship.cool = .2; A.sfx('shoot', { vol: .35 }); }\n      }\n      for (const s of shots) s.y -= 270 * dt; shots = shots.filter(s => s.y > -10);\n      const sx = Math.sin(sway * 1.2) * 12;\n      let formed = 0;\n      for (const f of foes) {\n        if (f.state === 'in' || f.state === 'dive') {\n          f.d += FLY * (1 + wave * .04) * dt; if (f.d < 0) continue;\n          const p = f.path.at(f.d), u = f.state === 'in' ? Math.min(1, f.d / f.path.length) : 0; f.x = p.x + sx * u * u; f.y = p.y; f.a = p.angle;\n          if (f.d >= f.path.length) { if (f.state === 'dive') { f.state = 'back'; f.y = -20; f.x = f.slot.x + sx; } else f.state = 'form'; }\n          if (f.state === 'dive' && f.y < ship.y - 50 && Math.random() < dt * (.7 + wave * .1)) bombs.push({ x: f.x, y: f.y, vx: (ship.x - f.x) * .35, vy: 125 });\n        } else if (f.state === 'back') { f.y += 90 * dt; f.x += (f.slot.x + sx - f.x) * Math.min(1, dt * 4); f.a = Math.PI / 2; if (f.y >= f.slot.y) f.state = 'form'; }\n        else { f.x = f.slot.x + sx; f.y = f.slot.y + Math.sin(sway * 3 + f.slot.x * .1) * 1.5; f.a = Math.PI / 2; formed++; }\n      }\n      if (live && formed > 3 && Math.random() < dt * (.45 + wave * .15)) { const c = foes.filter(f => f.state === 'form' && f.hp > 0); if (c.length) { const f = c[Math.floor(Math.random() * c.length)]; dive(f); if (f.kind === 'boss') for (const e of c.filter(e => e !== f && e.kind === 'b' && Math.abs(e.slot.x - f.slot.x) < 20).slice(0, 2)) dive(e); A.sfx('whoosh', { vol: .3 }); } }\n      for (const b of bombs) { b.x += b.vx * dt; b.y += b.vy * dt; } bombs = bombs.filter(b => b.y < FH + 10);\n      for (const s of shots) for (const f of foes) if (!s.hit && f.hp > 0 && f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(s.x - f.x) < 7 && Math.abs(s.y - f.y) < 6) { s.hit = true; if (--f.hp > 0) { A.sfx('bump'); P.sparks(X0 + f.x, Y0 + f.y, 4, 4); } else kill(f); }\n      shots = shots.filter(s => !s.hit); foes = foes.filter(f => f.hp > 0);\n      if (live) for (const o of [...bombs, ...foes]) if (Math.abs(o.x - ship.x) < 6 && Math.abs(o.y - ship.y) < 6) { dead = 1.8; P.explosion(X0 + ship.x, Y0 + ship.y, 4, .9, { sound: true, flash: false, shake: 2, freeze: false }); if (o.hp) kill(o); break; }\n      if (!foes.length && dead <= 0) newWave();\n    }\n    // the demo's pilot: of a step left, none and a step right, the first where no bomb or diving moth will be in the next\n    // half second (a bomb's way read ahead to the ship's row), preferring the way to the moth nearest above; firing when\n    // under one\n    const hitAt = (x, t) => bombs.some(b => { const k = (ship.y - b.y) / b.vy; return k > -.05 && k < t && Math.abs(b.x + b.vx * k - x) < 9; }) || foes.some(f => f.state === 'dive' && f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(f.y - ship.y) < 40 && Math.abs(f.x - x) < 12);\n    const botMove = () => {\n      const t = foes.find(f => f.state === 'dive' && f.y < ship.y - 50) || foes.filter(f => f.d >= 0).reduce((p, f) => !p || Math.abs(f.x - ship.x) < Math.abs(p.x - ship.x) ? f : p, null);\n      const want = t ? clamp((t.x - ship.x) / 10, -1, 1) : 0, ways = [want, 0, -1, 1].map(m => Math.round(m)), q = m => clamp(ship.x + m * 115 * .3, 10, FW - 10);\n      for (const m of ways) if (!hitAt(q(m), .8) && !hitAt((ship.x + q(m)) / 2, .4)) return m === Math.round(want) ? want : m;\n      return ship.x < FW / 2 ? 1 : -1;\n    };\n    const botFire = () => foes.some(f => f.d >= 0 && Math.abs(f.x - ship.x) < 8);\n    function layout() { FH = Math.max(270, game.H - 4); X0 = Math.round((game.W - FW) / 2); Y0 = Math.round((game.H - FH) / 2); }\n    function draw(r) {\n      layout(); const cl = classic(), x0 = X0, y0 = Y0;\n      if (cl) r.sky(['#000000', '#000000']); else {\n        SPACE[0].draw(r);\n        r.decal(g => {   // a ringed gas giant low in the field, lit from the upper right: the ring's far half, the planet's banded\n          // shading (discs stepped toward the light), the ring's near half\n          const [ox, oy] = r.w(0, 0), cx = Math.round(ox + x0 + FW * .24), cy = Math.round(oy + y0 + FH - 40), R = 40;\n          const ring = near => { for (let a = 0; a < TAU; a += .012) { if ((Math.sin(a) > 0) !== near) continue; for (const [k, c] of [[1.55, '#8a6aa8'], [1.7, '#c8a8e0'], [1.85, '#6a4a88']]) px.dot(g, cx + Math.cos(a) * R * k, cy + Math.sin(a) * R * k * .22, c); } };\n          ring(false);\n          ['#1a1030', '#2a1a46', '#3e2860', '#563a7a', '#704e94', '#8c66ac', '#a882c2'].forEach((c, k) => px.disc(g, cx + k * 1.4, cy - k * 1.4, R - k * 4.5, c));\n          for (let b = -2; b <= 2; b++) { const y = b * 12 + 3, hw = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, (R - 2) ** 2 - y * y)) - 3; px.blend(g, .16, 'normal', () => px.rect(g, cx - hw + 1, cy + y, hw * 2, 2, b % 2 ? '#2a1640' : '#e8c8a0')); }\n          ring(true);\n        });\n      }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Shell|class Settings|class Arcade|class Game|class Menu|_onBlur|visibilitychange|Shell \\\\{|ui.show|shell.show|settings.define' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -70 && rg -n 'shell\\\\.|E.Shell|settings\\\\.add|settings\\\\.define|settings.reset|menu.items|E.Arcade' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -90 && rg -n 'bridge|round.js|script src|limit|auto' vendor/hub/harness.html | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Shell|class Settings|class Arcade|class Game|class Menu|_onBlur|visibilitychange|Shell \\\\{|ui.show|shell.show|settings.define' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -70 && rg -n 'shell\\\\.|E.Shell|settings\\\\.add|settings\\\\.define|settings.reset|menu.items|E.Arcade' vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md | head -90 && rg -n 'bridge|round.js|script src|limit|auto' vendor/hub/harness.html | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"838:    on(document, 'visibilitychange', () => { if (document.hidden) all(q => q.clear()); });\n2308:class Game {\n2560:    on(document, 'visibilitychange', () => { if (document.hidden) this._autoPause('focus'); this.audio._background(document.hidden && !this.settings.background); });   // a hidden page sleeps its soun [... omitted end of long line]\n3087:class Settings {\n3772:  if (!this.settings.spec('playerBindings')) this.settings.define({ key: 'playerBindings', group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { for (const p of g.players.slice(1) [... omitted end of long line]\n9269:class Menu {\n9345: *      ui.show('title', { name: 'VESPER', subtitle: 'The Ninth Bell', actions: [['Enter the district', start]] });\n9349: *      ui.toast('Checkpoint', 'The ledger is yours'); ui.show('results', { title: 'The names are safe', stats, medals })\n9415:class Shell {\n9422:   * - screens: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n10413:    click: 'mouse', dblclick: 'mouse', contextmenu: 'mouse', input: 'value', change: 'value', resize: 'resize', visibilitychange: 'hidden',\n10415:  const ON_DOC = ['visibilitychange', 'fullscreenchange', 'webkitfullscreenchange'];\n10650:class Arcade {\n88:- 1184 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n91:- 1243 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n555:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n575:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its  [... omitted end of long line]\n577:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n637:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game,  [... omitted end of long line]\n1168:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1186:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HT [... omitted end of long line]\n1187:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) f [... omitted end of long line]\n1188:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1189:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard [... omitted end of long line]\n1190:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1191:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1192:- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n1193:- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n1194:- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n1195:- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n1196:- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n1197:- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n1198:- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\n1199:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n1200:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n1201:- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells blac [... omitted end of long line]\n1202:- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\n1203:- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n1204:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (stri [... omitted end of long line]\n1205:- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n1206:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1207:- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n1208:- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n1209:- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\n1210:- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\n1211:- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\n1245:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a ga [... omitted end of long line]\n1628:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1718:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n12:  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\n23:  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\n26:  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\n29:  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\n37:  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n61:    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\n66:import { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\n67:import { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n72:const auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\n170:  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\n181:  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(),  [... omitted end of long line]\n183:  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\n192:    limitMs,\n211:    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; autoplay; gamepad; pointer-lock';\n226:    cell.bridge = createBridge({\n238:      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\n240:        if (id !== cell.bridge?.me) return;\n246:    endpoint.onMessage((from, env) => cell.bridge.fromNet(from, env));\n247:    cell.detach = attachFrame(frame, (msg) => cell.bridge.fromGame(msg));\n258:    if (!auto && performance.now() >= state.splashUntil) return releaseRound(state);\n275:  const ready = state.cells.filter((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => c.bridge.me);\n277:    if (cell.gone || !cell.bridge.showsCard) continue;\n282:    cell.bridge.card(card);\n302:  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\n345:    bits.push(`↑${cell.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${cell.bridge.stats.received}`);\n350:  if (s.gate && !s.released) lines.push(`Card: ${state.cells.some((c) => c.bridge.showsCard) ? 'the game’s own, ' : ''}${state.splashUntil ? `${Math.max(0, Math.ceil((state.splashUntil - performance.n [... omitted end of long line]\n371:  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\n377: * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\n483:        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\n484:          state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n486:        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\n487:          remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\n492:      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\n493:        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${c.bridge.stats.received}`).join(' '));\n502:      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\n503:        record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason}), host ${record.hostId}, server sent ${serverCell.bridge.stats.sent}` : 'no end');\n511:    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\n512:    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\n544:if (auto) conformance();\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9340,9675p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '3087,3188p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '10650,10755p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9340,9675p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '3087,3188p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '10650,10755p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":" *    minimap) a modern adaptation would otherwise write by hand in HTML and CSS. It shows game state and holds none:\n *    the game passes values in every step and callbacks for the buttons, and it reaches the game only through those and\n *    input actions (a button's act is tapped, as input.bindButtons presses one).\n *      const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#d9b77c' }, settings: { items: ['sound', 'volume', 'motion'] },\n *        screens: { pause: { text: () => objective.title }, help: { keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ['SPACE', 'Climb']] } } });\n *      ui.show('title', { name: 'VESPER', subtitle: 'The Ninth Bell', actions: [['Enter the district', start]] });\n *      every step: ui.hud({ objective: { title, text, at: ledger, from: hero }, status: 'UNSEEN',\n *        bars: [{ value: hp, max: 5, kind: 'pips' }], prompt: near && { key: 'E', label: 'Take the ledger', progress },\n *        minimap: { map, at: hero, markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'diamond' }] } });\n *      ui.toast('Checkpoint', 'The ledger is yours'); ui.show('results', { title: 'The names are safe', stats, medals })\n *    With a pause screen, it opens while game.paused and Resume unpauses. Keys, d-pad, stick and touch move the focus\n *    (up / down / left / right turn a slider or a choice, confirm presses, cancel goes back, pause or Start closes the\n *    menu); while a screen is open the game's input is held back. It honors reduced motion and the safe-area insets, CSS\n *    variables theme it (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont), and a headless game keeps its screens'\n *    names and draws nothing.\n *    THE STANDARD MENU: every game gets one (new E.Game makes this shell for itself, and a game's own E.Shell takes over\n *    from it): the pause screen (Resume, the game's items, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Save session while the\n *    page is recorded, Quit to title with a confirmation), the settings screen (Display, Sound, Comfort and the game's own settings, from game.settings) and the\n *    controls screen (every action's keys and buttons, rebound by pressing the new one, conflicts said before anything\n *    changes; the controller's dead zone, aim, symbols and vibration; the touch buttons' side, size and opacity; restore\n *    defaults). new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [...], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill:\n *    false }, quit: 'title' } }) adjusts it; menu: false, or new E.Shell(game, { standard: false }), leaves it out.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst SHELL_CSS = `.esh{position:fixed;inset:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:20;font:14px/1.45 var(--font);color:var(--ink);--sat:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);\n--pt:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));--pr:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-right,0px));--pb:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));--pl:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-left,0px))}\n.esh *{box-sizing:border-box}.esh [hidden]{display:none!important}.esh p{margin:4px 0 0;white-space:pre-line}\n.esh h1,.esh h2{font-family:var(--title);font-weight:600;margin:2px 0 0;line-height:1.05}.esh h2{font-size:26px}\n.esh-pan{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:10px 13px;box-shadow:0 8px 28px #0009}\n.esh-k{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}.esh-m{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\n.esh-obj{position:absolute;left:var(--pl);top:var(--pt);max-width:min(330px,58vw)}.esh-obj b{font:600 17px var(--title);display:block}\n.esh-dist{color:var(--accent);font-size:12px;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:.06em}\n.esh-vit{text-align:right;min-width:120px}.esh-hb{display:flex;gap:6px;pointer-events:auto}.esh-hb button{padding:6px 10px;font-size:11px;background:var(--paper)}\n.esh-st{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em}.esh-st i{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;margin-right:6px;background:var(--c)}\n.esh-pips{margin-top:5px}.esh-pips i{display:inline-block;width:9px;height:9px;margin-left:4px;transform:rotate(45deg);background:var(--c,var(--danger))}.esh-pips i.off{opacity:.22}\n.esh-bar{height:4px;background:#ffffff1c;border-radius:2px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:6px}.esh-bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--c,var(--accent));transition:width .2s}\n.esh-cnt{margin-top:6px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.esh-cnt b{color:var(--ink);margin-left:5px}\n.esh-toast{position:absolute;left:50%;top:var(--pt);transform:translate(-50%,calc(-100% - 30px));transition:transform .35s;max-width:min(420px,80vw);text-align:center}.esh-toast.on{transform:translate(-50%,0)}\n.esh-tut{position:absolute;left:var(--pl);bottom:var(--pb);max-width:min(330px,62vw);pointer-events:auto;padding-right:30px}\n.esh-x{position:absolute;right:6px;top:4px;background:none!important;border:0!important;color:var(--muted)!important;padding:2px 6px!important;font-size:16px!important}\n.esh-pr{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 44px);transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;min-width:200px}\n.esh kbd{font:700 12px var(--font);border:1px solid var(--accent);border-bottom-width:2px;border-radius:4px;padding:2px 7px;color:var(--accent)}\n.esh-tip{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 100px);transform:translateX(-50%);text-align:center;border-color:var(--danger)}\n.esh-col{position:absolute;right:var(--pr);top:var(--pt);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:8px}.esh-place{text-align:right;font:italic 13px var(--title);color:var(--muted)}\n.esh-mini{position:absolute;right:var(--pr);bottom:var(--pb);width:min(176px,28vw);border-radius:6px;border:1px solid var(--line);pointer-events:auto;cursor:pointer}\n.esh-keys{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:var(--pb);transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:14px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;background:rgba(8,6,14,.62);padding:5px 12px;border-radius:8px}.esh-keys kbd{margin-right:4px}\n@media (pointer:coarse){.esh-keys{display:none}}@media (max-width:640px){.esh-obj{max-width:calc(100vw - 214px)}.esh-toast{left:var(--pl);right:var(--pr);top:auto;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 124px);max-width:none;transform:translateY(calc(100% + 160px))}.esh-toast.on{transform:none}\n.esh-pr{bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 196px)}.esh-tip{bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 262px)}}\n.esh-sh{position:absolute;inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#04060acc;pointer-events:auto;padding:calc(var(--pt) + 46px) var(--pr) var(--pb) var(--pl);animation:esh-in .25s;touch-action:pan-y}.esh-ttl{padding-top:var(--pt)}\n.esh-sh *{touch-action:pan-y}.esh-sh input{touch-action:auto}\n.esh .esh-nav{position:fixed;top:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));z-index:2;width:44px;height:44px;min-height:44px;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:0;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(8,8,18,.6);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.3);pointer-events:auto}\n.esh-nav.x{right:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-right,0px))}.esh-nav.bk{left:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-left,0px))}.esh-sw{transition:transform .2s,opacity .2s}\n.esh-mod{width:min(460px,100%);max-height:100%;overflow:auto;padding:22px 24px}.esh-wide{width:min(760px,100%)}\n.esh-ttl{place-items:center start;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#04060aee,#04060a99 50%,#04060a00 85%)}.esh-ttl>div{max-width:min(520px,92vw);padding-left:4vw}\n.esh-ttl h1{font-size:clamp(44px,10vw,92px);letter-spacing:.07em}.esh-sub{font:italic 20px var(--title);color:var(--accent);margin-top:6px}\n.esh-btns{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;margin-top:18px}.esh-tags{display:flex;gap:10px;margin-top:18px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--muted)}\n.esh button{font:600 13px var(--font);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink);background:#ffffff0f;border:1px solid #ffffff2c;border-radius:4px;padding:10px 14px;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}\n.esh button.pri{background:var(--accent);border-color:var(--accent);color:#16130e}.esh button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}\n.esh button:focus-visible,.esh input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}\n.esh-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.esh-row button{min-width:64px;text-align:center}\n.esh input[type=range]{accent-color:var(--accent);width:140px}.esh-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:6px 14px;margin-top:12px;align-items:center}\n.esh-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(96px,1fr));gap:10px;margin:16px 0 8px}.esh-stats b{display:block;font:600 24px var(--title)}\n.esh-stats small{color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em}.esh-med{display:inline-block;margin:6px 6px 0 0;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--accent);font-size:12px}.esh-med.off{opacity:.35;border-color:var(--muted)}\n.esh-sec{margin-top:14px}.esh-emb{font-size:34px;color:var(--accent);text-align:center}.esh-map{width:100%;margin-top:12px;border-radius:4px;cursor:crosshair;display:block}\n.esh-still,.esh-still *{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.esh *{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}\n.esh-cornered .esh-col{top:calc(var(--pt) + 50px)}.esh-sh button{min-height:44px}.esh-row{flex-wrap:wrap}.esh-row>span{flex:1 1 150px}.esh-row small{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:11px;line-height:1.3}\n.esh-ctl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}.esh output{min-width:46px;text-align:right;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.esh-sel{min-width:136px;text-align:center!important}.esh input[type=range]{height:30px}.esh-status{min-height:20px;margin-top:8px;color:var(--accent);font-size:12px}\n.esh-bind{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr minmax(92px,auto) minmax(92px,auto);gap:6px 10px;align-items:center;margin-top:8px}.esh-bind small{color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;text-align:center}\n.esh-bind button{text-align:center;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:.02em;font-size:12px;padding:8px 10px}.esh-bind button.cap{outline:2px dashed var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}\n@keyframes esh-in{from{opacity:0}}`;\nconst SHELL_THEME = { ink: '#f1e8d6', paper: 'rgba(14,18,22,.86)', accent: '#d9b77c', muted: '#a49d8c', danger: '#e8836a', line: 'rgba(217,183,124,.3)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'Georgia, serif' };\n/** the settings screen's groups, in order (the standard ones; a game's own are 'Game' unless they name another) */\nconst SHELL_GROUPS = ['Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort'];\n/** 'menuUp' -> 'Menu up': an action's name on the controls screen when the game gives none */\nconst actionName = a => { const t = String(a).replace(/([a-z])([A-Z0-9])/g, '$1 $2').replace(/[_-]+/g, ' ').toLowerCase(); return t.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + t.slice(1); };\nclass Shell {\n  /**\n   * new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings',\n   * meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n   * - theme: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole\n   *   interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) for a TV across a room; tv: true picks one by\n   *   the window's width (14 px text at 875 px, up to 30 at 1,875)\n   * - screens: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n   * - settings: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max,\n   *   step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n   * - store, meters: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n   * - standard: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the\n   *   settings' groups)\n   */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    if (game.shell && game.shell._sys && !o.system) game.shell.dispose();   // the game's own shell takes over from the engine's\n    /** game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game) */\n    this._game = game; this._o = o; this.root = null; this._stack = []; this._keep = new Set(); this._held = new Set(); this._last = {};\n    this._sys = !!o.system; this._std = o.standard !== false && game.o.menu !== false;\n    const old = store.get(o.store || 'shell-settings', null) || {}, S = game.settings;   // (settings saved by an older version are kept)\n    for (const it of this._items()) if (!S.spec(it.key)) { if (S._raw[it.key] === undefined && old[it.key] !== undefined) S._raw[it.key] = old[it.key]; S.define(Object.assign({ group: 'Game' }, it)); }\n    for (const k of ['sound', 'volume', 'motion']) if (S._raw[k] === undefined && old[k] !== undefined && this._items().some(it => it.key === k)) S.set(k, old[k]);\n    if (o.settings && o.settings.onChange) S.onChange = k => o.settings.onChange(S, k);\n    game.shell = this;\n    if (!this._sys && this._pauseSpec()) game.pauseOverlay = false;\n    if (game.headless || typeof document === 'undefined') return;\n    // rebinding: the next key or mouse button goes to the action being bound (before the game's own listeners see it)\n    const signal = game._abort ? game._abort.signal : undefined;\n    addEventListener('keydown', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c) return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); if (e.code === 'Escape') this._capEnd('Not changed.'); else if (c.device === 'keys' && !e.repeat) this._capBind(e.code); }, { capture: true, signal });\n    addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c || c.device !== 'keys' || e.pointerType !== 'mouse') return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); this._capBind('Mouse' + e.button); }, { capture: true, signal });\n    addEventListener('wheel', e => { const c = this._cap; if (!c || c.device !== 'keys' || !e.deltaY) return; e.preventDefault(); e.stopImmediatePropagation(); this._capBind(e.deltaY < 0 ? 'WheelUp' : 'WheelDown'); }, { capture: true, signal, passive: false });\n    if (!document.getElementById('esh-css')) { const st = document.createElement('style'); st.id = 'esh-css'; st.textContent = SHELL_CSS; document.head.appendChild(st); }\n    const r = this.root = this._el('div', 'esh' + (game._corner ? ' esh-cornered' : '')), th = Object.assign({}, SHELL_THEME, o.theme);   // (the top-right column starts below the corner's buttons)\n    for (const k in th) r.style.setProperty('--' + (k === 'titleFont' ? 'title' : k), th[k]);\n    if (th.font && /\\d|\\b(bold|italic|normal|oblique)\\b/.test(th.font)) warn('shell:font', 'E.Shell theme.font is a family (\"Georgia, serif\"), not a CSS shorthand (\"' + th.font + '\"): the size comes from theme.scale');\n    const K = th.scale !== undefined ? th.scale : o.tv ? () => clamp(innerWidth * .016, 18, 30) / 14 : 1;   // (for ten feet: the whole interface that many times, still filling the window)\n    if (K !== 1) { const fit = () => { const k = Math.max(.25, +(typeof K === 'function' ? K(window) : K) || 1); Object.assign(r.style, { transform: 'scale(' + k + ')', transformOrigin: '0 0', inset: 'auto', left: '0', top: '0', width: 100 / k + 'vw', height: 100 / k + 'vh' }); }; fit(); addEventListener('resize', fit, { signal }); }\n    const host = document.body; host.appendChild(r);\n    const E2 = (cls, parent = r, tag = 'div') => { const e = this._el(tag, cls); e.hidden = true; parent.appendChild(e); retu