| Terminal audio lifecycle review and bus checks | Audio / session lifecycle | A later gesture could resume a suspended audio context after end. Terminal master mute persists; input is ignored after termination and a new standalone run deliberately restores the saved preference. |\n| 5 | Guest input cadence review and real room brake check | Multiplayer input | A brake edge could fall between 12 Hz sends. Inputs are now collected every fixed step, with the accumulated edge sent at packet cadence. |\n| 6 | Developer slider review and units assertions | Usability | Native formatting showed short times as percentages. Explicit units now take precedence. |\n| 7 | Six-character picker focus review and controller navigation assertion | Controller usability | Redrawing a changed character moved focus to the first column. The selected column is now retained after click or left/right changes. |\n| 8 | Credits/Help content bounds and controller navigation | Controller information access | Long static pages opened scrolled to bottom; the native Help entry could be empty. Information is paginated with compact native navigation; the complete custom flight school is the pause/title entry. |\n| 9 | Hosted/local settings review | Multiplayer usability | Local assistance switches were visible during authoritative network play despite not changing the shared rules. Session UI now hides those switches and exposes applicable local presentation settings. |''')\ns=s.replace('Failed dependent tests are not separate defects.','Failed dependent tests are not separate defects. Additional fixture corrections: harness \"'`play` is milliseconds, CSS-transformed `innerText` differs from underlying headings, and real CDP touch pointers are required for pointer capture. These are not counted as game defects.'\"')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"seconds\": 367.8833333331631,\n  \"score\": 3200,\n  \"stats\": {\n    \"ships\": 200,\n    \"intercepts\": 172,\n    \"hits\": 1,\n    \"brakes\": 17,\n    \"bonus\": 560\n  },\n  \"seen\": [\n    \"wave0\",\n    \"dart\",\n    \"wave1\",\n    \"mine\",\n    \"wave2\",\n    \"roller\",\n    \"wave3\",\n    \"hunter\",\n    \"wave4\",\n    \"wave5\",\n    \"wave6\",\n    \"wave7\",\n    \"boss0\",\n    \"boss1\",\n    \"boss2\"\n  ],\n  \"maxSnapshotBytes\": 1844,\n  \"seed\": 1982,\n  \"health\": [\n    3\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib\nroot=Path('.');Path('../build-config.json').rename('build-config.json')\nfor file in ['tests/browser.py','tests/network.py','tests/smoke.py']:\n p=Path(file);s=p.read_text().replace('(root.parent / \\\"build-config.json\\\")','(root / \\\"build-config.json\\\")');s=s.replace('groups.add(page.locator(\\\".esh-mod h2\\\").inner_text())','groups.add(page.locator(\\\".esh-mod h2\\\").text_content())');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tools/build.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace('path.join(work, \\\"build-config.json\\\")','path.join(root, \\\"build-config.json\\\")');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tests/packaging.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace('path.join(work, \\\"build-config.json\\\")','path.join(root, \\\"build-config.json\\\")');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');x=json.loads(p.read_text())\nx['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless state and legitimate solo/four-pilot campaign runs; final-bundle Chromium, WebKit and Firefox; standard-pad stub, touch and narrow-screen profiles; OfflineAudioContext signal/mute checks; four Hub conformance scenarios; real two-context PeerJS/WebRTC room lifecycle. No physical pad, real iOS hardware or subjective listening.'\nx['sourceInformation']['animation']='Native E.Path Catmull arrivals, E.sprite / E.anim hulls, procedural banking, recoil, expressive mask and phase choreography; native particles and lighting.'\nx['sourceInformation']['tech']='JavaScript / Canvas 2D / Web Audio; my-3D2dge 0.89.1 at 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691 (focused settings, scaling and units patches); Hub v1 / client 1.4.0 at 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869, unchanged; PeerJS 1.5.5 / WebRTC; Node 24.'\nx['testingFeedback']=[\n '9 distinct defects found and fixed; the issue ledger records each. Test-fixture errors and duplicate failures are excluded.',\n '1 game-breaking issue: a narrow, low-density screen could crop the defense lane. Other defects affected input, menus, audio lifecycle or developer usability.',\n 'The legitimate full-campaign action playthrough: all eight waves, all four weapon families, every boss phase and a single victory, without invulnerability or phase skips. The packaged browser run verifies the real integration too.',\n 'Boot-only checks; they detect loading faults but miss late campaign behavior and multiplayer lifecycle errors.'\n]\nx['engineFeedback']=[\n 'The dependency-free pixel renderer, native paths, animation, lighting, shell and exact headless stepping form a useful coherent base.',\n 'The arcade service uses alternating turns and three-letter initials; shared co-op and six-letter records needed custom rules. Native static shell pages also needed pagination for pad readability.',\n 'A deterministic serializable authoritative campaign world and a common action/snapshot protocol for Hub and standalone rooms.',\n 'Keeping native menus, audio lifecycle and local focus handling compatible with a shared world that continues running.',\n 'Added session-only settings (persist:false), hidden developer rows, fractional fitting for narrow/high-density displays, and unit-aware slider formatting. Only the bundled full engine is patched. The Hub client is unchanged.',\n 'Add an official shared-world arcade kit with compact snapshots, session-only tuning and controller-readable paged information screens.'\n]\nx['promptFeedback']=[\n 'Concrete mechanics, complete-flow requirements and executable acceptance checks made the intended adaptation clear.',\n 'PLAN.md specifies an ultra planning configuration while TASK.md supplies this max build identity; TASK.md was used for the actual model, filename and delivery metadata.',\n 'Completing the campaign, controller-first presentation and two real network environments in one independently runnable HTML.',\n 'Provide a machine-readable acceptance checklist and one small canonical shared-world example alongside the prose.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(x,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nmanifest={'engine':{'version':'0.89.1','commit':'8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691','patched':True},'hub':{'protocol':1,'client':'1.4.0','commit':'35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869','gitBlob':'472495d5a5939531220e8e0b626bc4be9146102b','sha256':hashlib.sha256(Path('vendor/hub/session.js').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'modified':False},'peerjs':{'version':'1.5.5','sha256':hashlib.sha256(Path('vendor/peerjs-1.5.5.min.js').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'license':'MIT'}}\nPath('vendor/revisions.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome check --write --javascript-linter-enabled=false --css-linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false --javascript-formatter-indent-style=space --javascript-formatter-indent-width=2 src tools tests/state.mjs tests/packaging.mjs\nruff check --fix --ignore BLE001,B023,S110 tests\nruff format tests\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet\nnode tools/test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"Checked 11 files in 32ms. No fixes applied.\nAll checks passed!\n3 files left unchanged\nFAIL controller-readable pages contain all information and instructions\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022729__x13156c/work/Attack-of-the-Time-Bandit-Boss-Attack-of-the-Timelord-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022729/tests/browser.py\", line 17, in check\n    value = fn()\n  File \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022729__x13156c/work/Attack-of-the-Time-Bandit-Boss-Attack-of-the-Timelord-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-022729/tests/browser.py\", line 315, in about\n    expect(fit, \"credits page clips static content at page \" + str(i))\n    ~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-022729__x13156c/work/Attack-of-the-Time-Bandit-Boss-Atta